{# Two pieces of rich text, the second shown only when the reader asks for it.

Expects:

* value.intro - Rich text, always shown
* value.extra - Rich text, behind the control

`details` rather than a button and a script: the browser already knows how to
open and close it, announce it to a screen reader and reach it from a keyboard,
so the block works before any JavaScript loads and still works if none does.

`details` gives no way to change the summary text when it opens, so both words
are in the markup and the stylesheet shows whichever fits the state.
#}
{% if value.config.anchor %}
<a name="{{value.config.anchor}}"></a>
{% endif %}
<div class="expanding-richtext">
    <div class="expanding-richtext__intro">
        {{ value.intro|rich_text }}
    </div>

    <details class="expanding-richtext__more">
        <summary class="expanding-richtext__toggle">
            <span class="expanding-richtext__label expanding-richtext__label--shut">{% trans %}Read more{% endtrans %}</span>
            <span class="expanding-richtext__label expanding-richtext__label--open">{% trans %}Show less{% endtrans %}</span>
        </summary>

        <div class="expanding-richtext__extra">
            {{ value.extra|rich_text }}
        </div>
    </details>
</div>
